1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,010
Listen to a talk in an architecture class.

2
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:05,156
W:

3
00:00:05,156 --> 00:00:12,030
The Eastgate Center in Harare, Zimbabwe, is a mixing complex combining retail spaces and offices.

4
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:16,214
When the architect Mick Pierce was asked to design the building in the early

5
00:00:16,214 --> 00:00:19,090
1990s, he faced a big challenge.

6
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:23,770
How to keep all its shops and offices cool without traditional air conditioning

7
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:26,260
and do it during an economic crisis.

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,753
Energy costs were high,

9
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:32,090
and importing advanced air conditioners was impossible.

10
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:36,120
To solve this dilemma Pierce looked to termite mounds.

11
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:39,210
Termites are insects that live in large colonies.

12
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:43,170
They build big mounds on the ground throughout the African savannah.

13
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:48,249
The mounds are amazing structures, summarizing 3 m above ground

14
00:00:48,249 --> 00:00:51,240
and extend another one to 3 m below the ground.

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:56,523
The underground chambers connect to the above-ground chimneys through a maze of tunnels,

16
00:00:56,523 --> 00:01:00,260
and this entire system works like natural climate control.

17
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:03,557
Warm air rises and escapes through the top,

18
00:01:03,557 --> 00:01:06,110
while cooler air flows in from below.

19
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:10,432
The thick walls of soil and clay absorb heat during the day

20
00:01:10,432 --> 00:01:12,120
and release it at night.

21
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:20,210
Termites fine-tune airflow by opening and closing vents, adding or removing soil to enlarge or seal passages.

22
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:23,240
On hot days, they open more vents for cooling.

23
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,260
At night, they close them to keep warm.

24
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:29,120
Then Pierce borrowed these ideas.

25
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:33,839
The Eastgate Center's walls are made from thick materials like concrete and brick,

26
00:01:33,839 --> 00:01:39,200
and there's a system of ducts and adjustable louvers throughout the building to mimic those vents.

27
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:46,060
The result, a building that uses far less energy than its conventional counterparts.
